Now tell me what is RAG

RAG is one of those concepts that sounds fancy but the core idea is actually simple — and it’s extremely useful when building real AI systems.

Let’s break it down like engineers. 👇

What RAG Is

RAG = Retrieval Augmented Generation

It means:

Instead of relying only on what the LLM learned during training, we retrieve relevant external data and give it to the model before generating the answer.

So the model answers using fresh / private / domain-specific data.

The Problem RAG Solves

LLMs have limitations:

1️⃣ They don't know your private data
(company docs, database, PDFs)

2️⃣ They can hallucinate

3️⃣ Training data becomes outdated

Example:

User: What is our insurance product surrender policy?

The LLM cannot know this unless you provide it.

This is where RAG comes in.

RAG Architecture

Classic pipeline:

User Question
     ↓
Embedding Model
     ↓
Vector Search (retrieve relevant docs)
     ↓
Send retrieved docs + question to LLM
     ↓
LLM generates answer
